UPDATE knowledge_global_actions
SET prompt_template = prompt_template || '

Scheduled job reporting contract: this cron run must always return OPENAB_KNOWLEDGE_CARDS_V1 followed by one JSON object with kind="retention", including when there are no Pending rows (items may then be empty). Add a job_run object with exactly: job_id="opencode-scheduled-source-retention"; a unique run_id; started_at and finished_at as timezone-aware ISO-8601 timestamps; status success, partial, or failed; note; and metrics containing the integer fields sources_scanned, items_scanned, protected_items, enqueued_items, pending_items, trash_due_items, trashed_items, failed_items. sources_scanned counts the configured sources fully attempted; items_scanned counts actual source entries examined; protected_items counts entries excluded by current protection rules; enqueued_items counts Queue rows created during this run; pending_items and trash_due_items count those Queue decisions observed after processing; trashed_items counts targets verifiably moved to Notion trash; failed_items counts entries whose required read, write, or verification failed. Use success only when all three sources and due Queue rows were processed completely and failed_items=0; use partial with a concise note when some results are usable; use failed with a note when the run produced no reliable result. If no trash tool is exposed, trashed_items must be 0 and due targets remain unchanged while their Queue rows become Trash Due. Do not claim that Queue insertion or Trash Due means deleted. The retention items array still contains only verified Decision=Pending rows, at most 5, so Discord can render Keep actions. Never invent counts, IDs, timestamps, or successful writes.'
WHERE action_id = 'retention_scan';

INSERT INTO schema_migrations(version) VALUES (10);
